cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its benchmark results in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "mode-resolved-calibration: mode-resolved calibration-confidence continuum for photometric inverse problems"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: dddsx3
    name: "GMX"
    email: "3570239187@qq.com"
version: 0.4.1
date-released: 2026-09-13
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/dddsx3/mode-resolved-calibration"
abstract: >-
  A Python library for mode-resolved calibration-confidence analysis of
  linearized inverse problems with structured nuisance. It computes
  Schur-complement delta-Fisher information, per-mode calibration-retention
  spectra, and certified bounds on calibration-precision allocation via an
  exact convex reformulation with Frank-Wolfe duality-gap certificates and
  an exact low-rank retention structure. Ships a frozen OpenIllumination
  benchmark (11 objects), independent headline-recomputation tests, and
  full reproducibility manifests.
keywords:
  - photometric inverse problems
  - calibration
  - Fisher information
  - Schur complement
  - spectral analysis
  - OpenIllumination